A||||2||4Banger Bandit||Does anyone else have this???||||
Z||000000||4Banger Bandit||09-08-1999||05:26 PM||||I just realized my car seems to have a noisy lifter.  Or maybe I just never heard it before.  I know that some engines are naturally noisy in the valvetrain, but is the 2.8 V6 one of them??  I fixed a noisy lifter on my Camaro before, but is there anything to look out for?  It looks like the intake needs to come off to get to the valve cover... Anyone else accomplished this?? ||||reg||
Z||000001||JIM GOOSE||09-09-1999||11:48 AM||||Youll need to remove all 3 parts of manifold one at a time & also valve covers to get to lifters. I rebuilt my 2.8 and put in all new valvetrain parts,Reed cam,new lifters,chromemoly pushrods,Magnum rockers,everything else new. It seems noisy for reasons beyond me & don't remember it being this way before. Cam lobe -lifter compatibility is important, might be able to take lifter apart and clean it if just one lifter.||||reg||
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-09-1999||04:11 PM||||I have an 85 2.8 v6 with 102000 miles on her.<BR>The engine does not have any noise except the exhaust rumble from a pinhole in a manifold, and a heat shield vibration.  I would say it needs to be torn down before serious engine problems occur.||||reg||
